;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; Three independent authorities are cited, not one: GLEIF (the global LEI
;; system), the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (the US federal deposit
;; insurer, which is the registration authority GLEIF names as having validated
;; the subsidiary bank's LEI), and the Securities and Exchange Commission (the
;; US federal securities regulator this entity files with).
;;
;; The FDIC and SEC rows are what make this more than a GLEIF mirror. Two joins
;; are load-bearing and are checkable only against those authorities' own bodies:
;;
;;   * FDIC certificate 27314. GLEIF records the subsidiary Synchrony Bank as
;;     validated at RA000744 (= FDIC) under registration id 27314. The FDIC's
;;     own API, asked for CERT 27314, returns Synchrony Bank AND names its
;;     holding company as SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL. So the parent-child edge GLEIF
;;     asserts is corroborated by a regulator that does not source it from GLEIF.
;;
;;   * 777 Long Ridge Road. GLEIF gives this as the headquarters address; SEC
;;     EDGAR gives the same street as the filer's business address, from a
;;     filing chain that is independent of the LEI system.
;;
;; Substrings are chosen from the RAW response body. The FDIC and GLEIF spell
;; the same Utah street differently (170 W Election Rd vs 170 West Election
;; Road), so each row matches the spelling its own authority publishes rather
;; than a normalised form -- normalising here would hide which body was read.
;;
;; Deliberately NOT cited, and why:
;;
;;   * www.sec.gov (browse-edgar and /Archives) answers HTTP 403 to automated
;;     clients at the edge. Measured 2026-08-20 with three different user
;;     agents, including a descriptive one: all three 403. This is not a
;;     user-agent policy that could be satisfied by declaring traffic, so the
;;     HTML surface is left out. data.sec.gov, the SEC's data API, answers 200
;;     and is what the SEC rows below use.
;;   * opencorporates.com, which GLEIF's ocid field points at (us_de/3703204),
;;     serves an hCaptcha challenge instead of the record. Working around a
;;     CAPTCHA is out of bounds, so the row is left out rather than recorded as
;;     a citation the gate cannot check.
;;   * www.ffiec.gov (National Information Center) answers 403 likewise.
;;   * www.nyse.com/quote/XNYS:SYF answers 200 but renders via JavaScript; the
;;     delivered body contains no occurrence of the company name, so there is
;;     no substring a body check could honestly assert.
;;   * SEC EDGAR's submissions metadata carries stateOfIncorporation NY, which
;;     disagrees with GLEIF's US-DE jurisdiction and with the Delaware file
;;     number below. The disagreement is real and was measured, but adjudicating
;;     it needs the 10-K cover page, which sits behind the 403 above. It is
;;     recorded here as an open question rather than asserted as a citation.
;;   * www.synchrony.com's own Terms of Use is not a register and is not cited.
;;     80-data/public/tos.journal.edn keeps the archived text and its retrieval
;;     date.
;;
;; Independent third-party archive. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
;; sponsored by Synchrony Financial.

